The primary goals of web recon include:

Identifying assets - Target addresses, web pages, subdomains, technologies
Discovering hidden info - backups, config files, internal documentation
Analysing the attack surface - looking for possible vulnerabilities and weaknesses, look at tech used, configs, and possible entry points
Gathering Intelligence - collecting for attacks further up the chain/exploits and social engineering tasks. looking for key personnel, email addresses, behaviours.

Types of reconnaissance
active - actively looking for information, includes activities not done by typical users, so this may stand out to analysts
passive - blending in with normal traffic and analysing as far as possible. typically yields less information, but is harder to detect

